{"questions":[{"question_id":"gm5x4qpYa6KEna62","paperTitle":"AIEEE 2002","year":2002,"examDate":2002,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"chemical-bonding-and-molecular-structure","chapterGroup":"inorganic-chemistry","topic":"hybridization-and-vsepr-theory","type":"mcq","marks":4,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"a-square-planar-complex-is-formed-by-hybridisation-of-which-2002-marks-4-gm5x4qpya6kena62.htm","content":"A square planar complex is formed by hybridisation of which atomic orbitals ?","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"s, p<sub>x</sub>, p<sub>y</sub>, d<sub>xy</sub>"},{"identifier":"B","content":"s, p<sub>x</sub>, p<sub>y</sub>, d<sub>x<sup>2</sup> - y<sup>2</sup></sub>"},{"identifier":"C","content":"s, p<sub>x</sub>, p<sub>y</sub>, d<sub>z<sup>2</sup></sub>"},{"identifier":"D","content":"s, p<sub>x</sub>, p<sub>y</sub>, d<sub>yz</sub>"}],"correct_options":["B"],"explanation":"Hybridization of square planar complex is dsp<sup>2</sup> . \n<br><br><img class=\"question-image\" src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/Nei65R2IhiRlE43dA/wDpE9Ru6hJowYLZqOXM9UAQwkGFCJ/WnAXEIOLYL0xwvBA806L7U/image.png\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"AIEEE 2002 Chemistry - Chemical Bonding &amp; Molecular Structure Question 233 English Explanation 1\">\n<br><br>In square planar complex all 4 surrounding atoms and central atom are in the same plane and let this plane is x <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> y plane.  As it is dsp<sup>2</sup>  hybridized, so it has 1 d orbital, 1 s orbital and 2 p orbital.\n<br><br>s orbital is non-directional, so we just write it as s.   \n<br><br><img class=\"question-image\" src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/XnzRtccORUlVDXo5e/w3gYXvD6QCRMH9viU7w2gYmHR7F7x/sznjFuzvX8siL7kWLxnkft/image.png\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"AIEEE 2002 Chemistry - Chemical Bonding &amp; Molecular Structure Question 233 English Explanation 2\">\n<br><br>In p<sub>x</sub> the two lobes are along x-axis and in p<sub>y</sub> two lobes are along y-axis \n<br><br>One d orbital is d<sub>x<sup>2</sup> <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> y<sup>2</sup></sub>,  it means out of four lobes of d orbital two along x-axis and two along y-axis. \n<br><br><img class=\"question-image\" src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/eazV13ESqrrBRCgrU/2JEWeVlv5Own3bQJH84IknFoRSv8d/NYVhxNHnEKgAnYlywZM5qf/image.png\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"AIEEE 2002 Chemistry - Chemical Bonding &amp; Molecular Structure Question 233 English Explanation 3\"> "}]}